and as we hit the milestone of a million  people vaccinated here in clark county  it's important for women to alert their  doctor before getting a mammogram  denise valdez has the warning in today's  buddy check 8 report  chances are you've heard of the side  effects of maybe having a sore arm  fatigue fever after getting the cobit  vaccine  another symptom is swollen lymph nodes  they can appear on mammography and  ultrasound  days after vaccination and could be  mistaken  for breast cancer swollen lymph nodes  are the body's normal response to the  vaccine  it means your system is making  antibodies to fight the copin 19  infection but radiologists should keep  this side effect  in mind when viewing breast images in an  article published in clinical imaging  researchers featured four case studies  of women who had just received their  first shot  now in this image a 57 year old female  with a single enlarged  left lymph node was detected eight days  after receiving her first dose  in her left arm the swollen lymph node  is highlighted here in blue and red  however her right breast appears normal  overall data from the centers for  disease control and prevention  show 11.6 percent of vaccine recipients  experience adenopathy after one dose  and 16 do so after the second dose  the large lymph node typically appeared  within two to four  days after the vaccination so given the  likelihood this side effect will develop  in a significant number of patients  you really need to let the radiologist  know that you've had the vaccine  and when because it could impact your  diagnosis  for buddy check i'm denise valdez back  to you
 

